From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0385-mem-audit-04-bad-alloc-uploads.patch

Source: 0385-mem-audit-04-bad-alloc-uploads.patch
Moved by hand: applies unchanged once 0181 and 0382 are in

Core patch, on core16 (through 0181). Paths are the submodule's.

Same rule as 0181: the image keeps what it shows until the guest writes it again, and the session
goes on. EDEN_NX2_BAD_ALLOC_ENDS=1 in env.txt ends it as before. There is no separate switch: the
only change without it is on a bad_alloc, which ended the session.

Covered now: RefreshSparseLayers, RefreshSparseTiles and UploadWrittenLayers in RefreshContents,
and the RefreshSparseTiles that PrepareImage calls after backing an image whole.

0181's own try could not work for the swizzle scratch, for two reasons found here:

- GuestMemory::Read was noexcept and grows the scratch. A bad_alloc there is std::terminate, past
  any catch. Every upload giving it &swizzle_data_buffer goes through it when guest memory is not
  contiguous. Tested on the real headers: SIGABRT before, caught after.
- ScratchBuffer::resize_destructive set the new capacity before allocating. Caught, the buffer
  then claimed 8 MiB on a 1 MiB allocation and the next upload wrote past its end. Tested the same
  way. On success both orders do the same, with the same peak.

The two 0181 branches now share KeepContentsAfterBadAlloc, so the rule sits in one place.

Not covered: a bad_alloc in QueueAsyncUnswizzle's queue, in BindSparseLayers on the modification
path, or in the cold-hint list after the upload (all small), and the download paths: Read no longer
terminates there, but nothing catches it, so they end as they did.

Syntax-compiled for the PS5 target with warnings on, TextureCache instantiated for Vulkan and
OpenGL, through prepare-vulkan-port.py (same skipped anchors as before). Not built, not run on the
console.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/common/scratch_buffer.h b/src/common/scratch_buffer.h
index cad1506922..fcbd1a22c9 100644
--- a/src/common/scratch_buffer.h
+++ b/src/common/scratch_buffer.h
@@ -76,8 +76,10 @@ public:
     /// The previously held data will be destroyed if a reallocation occurs.
     void resize_destructive(size_type size) {
         if (size > buffer_capacity) {
+            // Allocate first: a caller that catches the failure must not be left with the new
+            // capacity on the old, smaller buffer, or the next resize writes past its end.
+            buffer = std::make_unique_for_overwrite<T[]>(size);
             buffer_capacity = size;
-            buffer = std::make_unique_for_overwrite<T[]>(buffer_capacity);
         }
         last_requested_size = size;
     }
